    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i was looking at my student loan statement and the principal isnt going down as much as i thought it would even though i pay the same amount every month. can u explain how the interest actually works with the balance?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sure! A loan’s balance is split into **principal** (the amount you borrowed) and **interest** (the cost of borrowing). Each monthly payment is first applied to any interest that accrued during that month; only the leftover amount reduces the principal. Because interest is calculated on the current balance, a steady payment often trims the principal slowly at first—especially if the interest rate is high—so the balance appears to drop only a little each month.",
      "source": "target",
