    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "so it's like the interest is basically eating the payment before it touches the loan? is there a specific point where it starts to speed up, or is it always gonna be this slow?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Exactly—interest “eats” the front of each payment. As the principal gradually shrinks, the interest charged each month gets smaller, so a larger slice of your constant payment starts to go toward principal. This acceleration happens automatically once the interest portion falls below the total payment; you’ll see the balance drop faster, but it’s still a gradual process unless you increase your payment or refinance to a lower rate.",
      "source": "target",
