    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "is there like any way to stop it from happening? i feel like i'm just fighting an uphill battle with these hidden costs.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You can fight back by:\n\n1. **Paying extra** (even a small amount each month) so more goes straight to principal.  \n2. **Refinancing** to a lower interest rate or longer term, which cuts the monthly interest charge.  \n3. **Making bi‑weekly payments**—you end up making one extra full payment each year, shaving interest off the balance.  \n\nThese strategies reduce the interest that “eats” your payment and help the principal shrink faster.",
      "source": "target",
